# Address-of in safe code (port of unsafe-gate.test.ts): `&(x)` inside a function
# BODY, with no pragma(Pragma.AllowUnsafe), must FAIL under BOTH compilers.
#
# This is the BODY-level gate, and it was blocked until 2026-08-12. The gate
# fires while evaluating main's body, where the def-eval swallow ate it, so the
# self-hosted compiler exited 0 and emitted a runnable no-op binary while TS
# rejected it (SELF-FAIL). It passes now because a `// Failed to transpile`
# marker reaching `__yo_user_main` is fatal — the swallow still eats the throw,
# but the statement it drops can no longer vanish silently. See
# issues/fixed/self-hosted-compile-swallows-undefined-call.md.
#
# stdout=ignore: the two compilers word the fatal differently (TS names the
# gate, the self-hosted binary names the untranspiled entry point). rc parity is
# the assertion — and the sibling ptr-type-safe-code case covers the
# signature-level gate the same way.
# stdout_keep_match (P2.5 step 15): this case previously used stdout=ignore,
# which ANY failure satisfied. The kept substring is the probe-verified
# SHARED diagnostic - both compilers must emit it, so the case asserts THE
# failure, not just A failure.
stdout_keep_match=produces a raw pointer \('\*\(T\)'\), which is not available in safe code
timeout=120
